-- title:
--   Linear growth of #(X/I^mX) in powers of q
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian ring, let $q$ be a prime number such that the quotient $R/qR$ of $R$ by the ideal generated by the image of $q$ is finite, let $I \subseteq R$ be an ideal with $q \in I$ (meaning the image of $q$ in $R$ lies in $I$), and let $X$ be an $R$-module that is finite, i.e. finitely generated, over $R$. The assertion is that there exist natural numbers $e$ and $C$ such that for every natural number $m$ the cardinality of the quotient module $X/(I^m \cdot X)$, formed as the quotient of $X$ by the submodule $I^m \bullet \top$, satisfies both
--   $$\#\bigl(X/I^mX\bigr) \le q^{me+C} \qquad\text{and}\qquad q^{me} \le \#\bigl(X/I^mX\bigr)\cdot q^{C},$$
--   the cardinalities being taken as `Nat.card`. The slope $e$ and the constant $C$ are uniform in $m$. Since `Nat.card` vanishes on infinite types and $q \ge 2$, the second inequality forces each of these quotients to be finite. Equivalently, $\log_q \#(X/I^mX) = me + O(1)$ with a single $e$ valid for all $m$.
--
--   This is a Hilbert–Samuel type result, stated in the two-sided form that suffices for index computations: over a ring that is finite modulo $q$ the $q$-logarithm of the order of $X/I^mX$ grows linearly in $m$ with an error bounded independently of $m$. It generalises the corresponding statement for $R$ itself in place of a finitely generated module, and is used for the ideal-power quotients of Hecke-type algebras and for the quotients $X/I^mX$ occurring in [`Ideal.card_quotient_pow_hilbertSamuel_linear_of_moduleFinite`](thm.html#Ideal.card_quotient_pow_hilbertSamuel_linear_of_moduleFinite) and [`Submodule.natCard_torsionBySet_pow_linear_of_finite_torsionBy`](thm.html#Submodule.natCard_torsionBySet_pow_linear_of_finite_torsionBy).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_natCard_quotient_pow_smul_top_linear_of_finite_quotient.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem Submodule.natCard_quotient_pow_smul_top_linear_of_finite_quotient
    (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] (q : ℕ) [Fact q.Prime]
    (hRq : Finite (R ⧸ Ideal.span {(q : R)}))
    (I : Ideal R) (hqI : (q : R) ∈ I)
    (X : Type*) [AddCommGroup X] [Module R X] [Module.Finite R X] :
    ∃ e C : ℕ, ∀ m : ℕ,
      Nat.card (X ⧸ (I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule R X))) ≤ q ^ (m * e + C) ∧
        q ^ (m * e) ≤ Nat.card (X ⧸ (I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule R X))) * q ^ C := by sorry
